the terrorists also targeted the seat of  american military power one of the  hijacked jetliners american airlines  flight 77 crashed into the pentagon  along with the 59 passengers and crew on  board  125 military and civilian personnel  inside were killed those victims will be  remembered at a ceremony at the pentagon  this morning cbs news national security  correspondent david martin is there  david good morning  good morning this will begin with the  reading of the names of those who  perished followed at 9 37 the incident  the plane hit the pentagon by a moment  of silence but i want to begin this  morning with the name of a survivor  retired army colonel marilyn wills  i was blown on the opposite side of the  room wheels was in a second floor  conference room directly in the plane's  path the loudest noise of an explosion  that i had ever heard the room  immediately got dark and smoke filled  the room  as i was crawling out the door someone  grabbed the back of my pants i said hold  on wherever i go you go don't let me go  i got you  her colleague was in dire straits she  said at one point she couldn't go any  further  because she had nylons on  and the nylons were sticking to her legs  they were melting on her legs  i totally get on my back i'll carry you  this is your escape room  this is my escape route from the era  this corridor has since been renovated  but this is what the pentagon looked  like after the plane struck you can't  see anything  it's dark  it's black it's full of smoke  this would be the windows she was trying  to get to that window but it was blast  resistant  when that window wouldn't break  i got mad at god you led me here  and now we're gonna die  because i came to a window that we can't  open  but god said not yet  not yet  and it opened  marilyn wills led five people including  lois stevens to safety through that  window  crawling through an inferno that left  offices looking like this she wanted to  go back and search for more but her  commanding officer ordered her out of  the building  after she climbed down marilyn willis  passed out and almost died on the way to  the hospital from all the smoke she had  inhaled she woke up three days  later to learn for the first time  that a plane had hit the pentagon  dana david thank you such a horrifying  day but those stories of courage  certainly also staying with us
 

